diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:2:7: `len` is not defined
  print(len(names))
        ^^^
Emerald has no `len` function. Write `names.count`, which works on a String, List, Set, or Dict.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:3:13: `int` is not defined
  const age = int(input("Age? "))
              ^^^
Emerald has no `int` function. Write `input("Age? ").to_int()` to read a whole number from a String; a Float has `to_int()` too.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:4:19: `str` is not defined
  print("age is " + str(age))
                    ^^^
Emerald has no `str` function. Write `age.to_string()`, or put the value in interpolation, as in `"#{age}"`.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:5:10: `range` is not defined
  for i in range(1, 6) {
           ^^^^^
Emerald has no `range` function. A range is written with `..<`, which stops before the end: `1..<6`.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:8:13: `True` is not defined
  var ready = True
              ^^^^
Emerald writes Bool values in lowercase: `true` and `false`.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:9:23: `null` is not defined
  var winner: String? = null
                        ^^^^
Emerald writes absence as `nothing`. A value that may be absent has an optional type, as in `String?`.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:10:1: `console` is not defined
  console.log("hello")
  ^^^^^^^
Emerald prints with `print`, as in `print("hello")`; `write` does the same without the line break.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:12:7: `sqrt` is not defined
  print(sqrt(x))
        ^^^^
Emerald has no `sqrt` function. A Float takes its own square root: `x.square_root()`.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:13:7: `max` is not defined
  print(max(age, 3))
        ^^^
Emerald has no `max` function. Write `Math.max(age, 3)` for two values.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:14:7: `read_line` is not defined
  print(read_line())
        ^^^^^^^^^
Emerald reads a line of input with `input()`, as in `input("Name? ")`, or `input_maybe()` when the end of input is expected.
diagnostics/foreign-builtin-names.em:15:1: `Kernel` is not defined
  Kernel.print("hi")
  ^^^^^^
Emerald has no `Kernel`. Its built-ins, such as `print` and `input`, are written bare.
